      "hints": [
        "The general term in $\\left(2x + \\frac{a}{x^2}\\right)^5$ is $\\binom{5}{r}(2x)^{5-r}\\left(\\frac{a}{x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}a^r x^{5-3r}$.",
        "Set $5 - 3r = -1 \\implies r = 2$.",
        "Equate $\\binom{5}{2}2^3 a^2 = 720$ and solve for $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write down the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x + \\frac{a}{x^2}\\right)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r}(2x)^{5-r}\\left(\\frac{a}{x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}a^r x^{5-3r}$$",
        "Set the power of $x$ equal to $-1$ to find the term in $\\frac{1}{x}$:\n$$5 - 3r = -1 \\implies 3r = 6 \\implies r = 2$$",
        "Calculate the coefficient and equate it to $720$:\n$$\\binom{5}{2}2^{5-2}a^2 = 10(8)a^2 = 80a^2 = 720$$\n$$a^2 = \\frac{720}{80} = 9 \\implies a = \\pm 3$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
